  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q59-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the values of $a$ so that $\\sin^4\\theta+\\cos^4\\theta=a$ has solutions.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac12\\le a\\le1$.\n\nUse $\\sin^4\\theta+\\cos^4\\theta=1-\\frac12\\sin^2 2\\theta$ and $0\\le\\sin^2 2\\theta\\le1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^4\\theta+\\cos^4\\theta&=(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)^2-2\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta\\\\\\sin^4\\theta+\\cos^4\\theta&=1-2(\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta)^2\\\\\\sin^4\\theta+\\cos^4\\theta&=1-\\frac12\\sin^2 2\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0\\le\\sin^2 2\\theta\\le1$,\n$$\\frac12\\le\\sin^4\\theta+\\cos^4\\theta\\le1.$$\nBoth endpoints are attained: $\\theta=\\frac\\pi4$ gives $\\frac12$, and $\\theta=0$ gives $1$. Hence the required values are $\\boxed{\\frac12\\le a\\le1}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
